{
  "id": "character-displacement",
  "term": "character displacement",
  "definition": "Character displacement is a pattern in which populations of closely related species differ more in certain traits when they live together than when they live apart. In this packet, reproductive character displacement refers to divergence in features and mate-related behavior that is linked to co-occurrence with a similar species.",
